.venv/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.pytest_cache/
.DS_Store

# Imported artefacts and anything derived from them. All of it is regenerable
# from scripts/import_data.py and scripts/build_splits.py, and the recipe corpus
# is 40MB+ — large enough to make a repository unpleasant and slow to clone.
#
# The leading slash is load-bearing. An unanchored `data/` matches a directory
# of that name at any depth, which silently excluded the ingredient_model/data
# source package — splits.py, text.py and recipes.py were absent from the
# repository entirely rather than merely uncommitted.
#
# `*` rather than a bare directory, because git will not re-include a file whose
# parent directory is excluded — the exception below only works if the directory
# itself is still walked.
/data/*

# Except the generation marker, which is the single source of truth for which
# corpus is canonical and which normaliser built it. It is a few hundred bytes,
# it is read by sanity_check.py and data/text.py, and it is stamped into every
# run manifest — so a checkout that cannot see it cannot interpret its own
# results.
!/data/GENERATION.json

# results/runs/ is deliberately NOT excluded. The weight matrices are dropped by
# the root .gitignore's *.npy rule, which leaves manifest.json and metrics.json
# tracked — so the leaderboard is versioned and any published number can be
# traced to the commit that produced it. Excluding the directory wholesale would
# throw the findings away along with the blobs.
results/*.json

# Holds the subscription id. Not a secret, but not something to commit either,
# and it differs per developer.
cloud/config.json
